import json
from pathlib import Path
q=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
# Execute only definitions from build_bank: never rewrite frozen v1 artifacts.
ns={};exec((q/'build_bank.py').read_text().split("write('benchmark-v1',rows)")[0],dict(__file__=str(q/'build_bank.py')),ns) if False else None
rows=json.loads((q/'bank-rows-v1.json').read_text())
def add(question,a,ref,novel):rows.append({'id':f'Q{len(rows)+1:02}','question':question,'expected_answer':a,'source_references':ref,'novelty':novel})
add('How are eligible Objective cards selected and distributed in standard three- or four-player setup, how is First Player chosen, and may Shaddam be chosen without CHOAM?', 'Omit Objectives whose 1–3P or 4/6P mark mismatches count; shuffle, each takes one random face up in supply. First Player is holder of marked Objective. Shaddam cannot be chosen without CHOAM.', 'Main pp4–5 / extraction 210–220,254–263','Objective eligibility and Leader restriction')
add('If the bank runs out of Solari, spice, water or sandworms, what happens? Contrast an empty personal troop supply, and state where resource payments go.', 'Bank resources and sandworms not limited; substitute conveniently. Cannot recruit troops from empty personal supply until returned. Resource gains come from bank and payments return to bank.', 'Main pp5,10,20 / extraction 273–279,535–539,1152–1154','Component exhaustion and bank destinations')
add('State all five round phases in order, when Conflict and hand cards are drawn, and what Recall does if Endgame is not triggered.', 'Round Start, Player Turns, Combat, Makers, Recall. Start reveals top Conflict face up atop previous remaining cards then each draws five. If no Endgame, recall Agents to Leaders, pass First Player clockwise and begin next round (two-player Rival exception).', 'Main pp8,15 / extraction 355–360,385–390,824–834','Round order and restart')
add('May you resolve board-space effects, Agent-box effects and Faction Influence in any order? Can you use that visit’s Influence to meet its entry requirement?', 'Resolve effects in any order after placement, but entry requirements and costs must be met before any effects. Cannot rely on Influence gained by the visit for its entry requirement.', 'Main p9 / extraction 403–409,439–452,482–489','Effect-order versus entry requirement priority')
add('Can an optional arrow cost be paid twice in an Agent turn? Which effects are normally optional or mandatory, including costs on Intrigue cards?', 'Only once per turn, except sandworm-doubled Conflict rewards. Most effects mandatory except may, optional arrow payment and black-X trash. Direct self-trash mandatory. All Intrigue conditions/costs required to play it.', 'Main pp9,20; FAQ p3 optional effects/paying a cost','Optional effect boundary and Intrigue exception')
add('Where may a new Spy be placed, what if all your Spies are already deployed, and what if its placement effect specifies an Agent-icon type?', 'Unoccupied observation post, from supply. If none in supply may first recall one of own Spies for no effect. Specified icon must connect to post or cannot place there.', 'Main p11 / extraction 588–605','Spy placement and exhaustion')
add('Can you Infiltrate your own occupied board space, use a Spy without playing a card, or recall two connected Spies to Gather Intelligence twice on one placement?', 'No to all. Infiltrate bypasses another player Agent; still play a card and meet entry costs/requirements. Two Spies can pay different effects (Infiltrate and Gather Intelligence), not duplicate Gather Intelligence.', 'Main p11; FAQ p4 Spies','Spy ownership and per-effect recall limits')
add('Who gets control bonuses when visiting Arrakeen, Spice Refinery or Imperial Basin, how is control transferred, and where does the defensive troop originate?', 'Winning respective Conflict puts control marker on flag replacing opponent. Controller receives 1 Solari at Arrakeen/Refinery or 1 spice at Basin whenever anyone including self visits. Reveal of controlled location Conflict permits one troop from supply directly to Conflict.', 'Main p10,p20 / extraction 491–506,1099–1103','Control transfer, repeated benefit and defense')
add('When two players tie for second in a three-player Conflict, what happens? What if players tie for third in four-player play, or three players tie for first?', 'Tied second each get third reward; winner keeps first and card, no other rewards. Tied third receive nothing. Three tied first each get second, no winner/card and no further rewards.', 'Main p14 / extraction 792–808','Remaining combat tie outcome branches')
add('At a normal three-player Conflict with three different positive strengths, which places receive rewards? What if a two-player game’s Rival is one of the participants?', 'Only first and second rewarded, third only used for a tie for second. Two humans plus standard Rival use the same two-/three-player reward rules; Rival competes normally.', 'Main p14; Supplements p5 Combat; FAQ p1 Conflict','Untied low-player-count rewards')
add('When can Plot, Combat and Endgame Intrigues be played, how are unplayed Intrigues kept and ordinary ones discarded, and what if the Intrigue deck is exhausted?', 'Plot during own Agent/Reveal turns, Combat during Combat with a unit, Endgame at game end. Unplayed face down separate from deck, owner may inspect; played resolved cards face up Intrigue discard. Exhaustion reshuffles Intrigue discard into new deck.', 'Main p7 / extraction 345–354; FAQ p2 Intrigue cards','Intrigue storage, timing and exhaustion')
add('Can you discard an Intrigue for an ordinary discard instruction? Where does an ordinary discard come from? How does Secrets choose which Intrigue is stolen?', 'Ordinary discard from hand and cannot be Intrigue unless specified. Secrets steals one random Intrigue from each opponent with four or more, in addition to drawing one from deck and gaining Bene Gesserit Influence.', 'Main p20 / extraction 1104–1106,1179–1181; Supplements p2; FAQ p2 discard','Discard type and theft threshold')
add('Which cards may a trash effect remove, where do ordinary and Reserve cards go, and is trashing optional? Does trashing The Spice Must Flow remove its acquired VP?', 'May trash own hand, discard or in-play card. Ordinary to box; Reserve back to its Reserve stack. Optional unless cost or direct self-trash. The Spice Must Flow acquire VP retained after trashing.', 'Main p20 / extraction 1185–1190; FAQ p4 The Spice Must Flow','Trash locations and persistent acquire VP')
add('When do acquire-box effects resolve, when do you reshuffle your deck, and can unused Persuasion be carried to another round?', 'Acquire effect once at acquisition not when later played. Reshuffle discard only when unable to draw due to empty deck then continue. Unspent Reveal Persuasion lost, never saved.', 'Main pp6,13,20 / extraction 311–317,704–730,1081–1084','Acquire triggers, reshuffle trigger and resource expiration')
add('What counts as in play for Fremen Bond, can two Bond cards activate one another regardless of play order, and when do they cease being in play?', 'Agent-turn and Reveal cards remain in play face up until Reveal Clean Up unless trashed earlier. Bond requires at least one other Fremen in play; two Bond cards can activate each other regardless of order.', 'Main p20 / extraction 1111–1117','In-play lifetime and Fremen Bond interaction')
add('Can Recall Agent return the Agent placed this turn, and when can the recalled Agent act again? Where does a retreated troop go, and may “retreat any number” mean zero?', 'Recall another Agent from board to Leader, not current-turn Agent; can use on later Agent turn same round. Retreat Conflict to garrison; any number permits zero.', 'Main p20 / extraction 1147–1157; FAQ p3 Retreat','Recall and retreat destinations and reuse')
add('When an effect grants two Influence with a freely chosen Faction, may it be split? What is required for an Alliance-icon effect or a minimum-Influence effect?', 'Choose one Faction, both Influence there (not split). Alliance effect requires holding shown Faction Alliance token; minimum-Influence effect requires at least shown value with shown Faction.', 'Main p20 / extraction 1086–1088,1118–1126','Effect eligibility and indivisible Influence')
add('If an Alliance holder loses Influence after being tied with two opponents, who receives the token? If the holder drops to 3 and no one has 4, what happens?', 'Former holder chooses one of previously tied opponents to receive token; holder loses Alliance VP and receiver gains it. Below 4 loses token; if no eligible 4+ player return token to board, losing its VP.', 'FAQ p1 Alliance','Alliance loss from retreating holder')
add('What happens to a card drawn during Reveal compared with one drawn after Reveal? What happens to a Plot Intrigue played earlier whose effect applies at Reveal?', 'During Reveal immediately reveal and use this turn; after Reveal keep until next round, then draw five extra. Plot effect for later Reveal stays face up until that Reveal, use then discard.', 'FAQ pp2–3 Intrigue cards/Reveal turn','Draw timing branches and delayed Plot duration')
add('May a “when you win a Conflict” Intrigue be played after tying for first? What if you receive such an Intrigue as a reward for an outright win?', 'Tie for first is not a win, cannot play. An appropriate Intrigue received as winning reward can be played immediately.', 'FAQ p4 When you win a Conflict','Win-trigger exception and newly gained card timing')
add('What if final VP, spice, Solari, water and garrison troops all remain tied, and may scores exceed 12?', 'Final tiebreaker is player who most recently took Reveal turn. Scores may exceed printed track maximum 12.', 'FAQ p2 Endgame; p4 Victory Points','Final tiebreaker and score boundary')
add('Can you delay completion of two held contracts for the same board space after visiting, and when in the Agent turn can their effects resolve?', 'Completion mandatory; all same-space contracts completed with one Agent placement. Their effects may resolve in any order with space and Agent-box effects; still must hold them at placement.', 'FAQ p1 contract; Main p16','Mandatory simultaneous contracts and effect ordering')
add('Under CHOAM does Shaddam begin with his set-aside Sardaukar contracts, when can he take one, and how long does his Signet Ring deployment restriction last?', 'No, not in possession at start. Sardaukar Commander allows acquiring set-aside Sardaukar contract instead of generally available one when taking a contract. Emperor of Known Universe restriction starts immediately with Signet Ring Agent placement and lasts that turn only.', 'Main p17; FAQ p3 Shaddam Corrino IV','Shaddam contract choice and restriction duration')
add('For Feyd, where does the Training token start and what happens at its last space? Which Jessica side begins face up and can Reverend Mother Jessica act on the flip turn?', 'Feyd starts leftmost Training space, stays forever on rightmost once reached. Lady Jessica side starts up, not Reverend Mother. Reverend Mother ability usable on flip turn.', 'Main p17 / extraction 957–964; FAQ p3 Reverend Mother Jessica','Leader setup and transition timing')
add('For Margot and Irulan does moving from 1 to 3 Influence count as reaching 2, can it trigger again later, and does descending through 2 count? Does Clean Up trigger Spacing Guild’s Favor discard ability?', 'Passing 2 upward counts, can repeat by losing then regaining Influence; descending does not count. Spacing Guild Favor triggers discard from hand, not in-play-to-discard Clean Up.', 'Main p17 / extraction 965–978','Threshold crossing and discard-source exception')
# Board-space coverage adds actual costs, choices, lasting effects; these were not covered by seed.
add('State Accept Contract and Dutiful Service’s Agent icons and effects with and without CHOAM, and whether both automatically advance a Faction track.', 'Accept Contract: Spice Trade, draw card plus contract or 2 Solari, no automatic Faction Influence. Dutiful Service: Emperor, one Emperor Influence plus contract or 2 Solari. Contract fallback if module off or all contracts taken.', 'Supplements p1','Nonfaction versus Faction contract spaces')
add('What do Arrakeen, Fremkit and Research Station each cost and provide, what Agent icons access them, and which are Combat spaces?', 'Arrakeen City free, troop and card, controller 1 Solari. Fremkit Fremen free, 1 Fremen Influence and card. Research Station City 2 water, two troops and two cards. All Combat.', 'Supplements pp1–2','Free versus paid card/recruit Combat spaces')
add('Compare Deep Desert and Hagga Basin’s entry costs, base spice and worm choices. Do you still collect bonus spice when choosing worms, and are Hooks spent?', 'Deep Desert 3 water, 4 spice OR two worms; Hagga 1 water, 2 spice OR one worm. Both collect all bonus spice even with worms. Worm choice requires Maker Hooks, not spent; cannot summon into Shield-Wall-protected Conflict.', 'Supplements pp1–2; Main p10; FAQ p2 Maker hooks','Maker choice excludes base spice but retains bonus')
add('For each Sietch Tabr option, state requirements and effects. Do you get a troop when choosing to remove the Shield Wall?', 'City access, 2+ Fremen Influence, no resource cost. Option one Hooks if needed, one troop, one water; option two one water and may remove wall. Option two gives no troop or Hooks. Combat space.', 'Supplements p2','Sietch mutually exclusive option branches')
add('How do High Council’s first and subsequent visits differ, what does each cost, when is its ongoing benefit used, and is it a Combat space?', 'Landsraad 5 Solari each visit. First Councilor to empty seat, +2 Persuasion each Reveal rest of game; later 2 spice, Intrigue, three troops. Not Combat, cannot normally deploy recruited troops.', 'Supplements p2','High Council persistent upgrade versus revisit rewards')
add('What does Swordmaster cost before and after anyone obtains one, how often may each player visit, and when can the new Agent be used? Does a Rival obtaining it lower human cost?', 'Landsraad 8 Solari before any Swordmaster, then 6; once per player per game. Third Agent from beside board onto Leader immediately usable same round and rest of game. Rival also lowers cost.', 'Supplements p2; FAQ p3 Rivals','Swordmaster dynamic cost and immediate action capacity')
add('State Imperial Privilege’s Agent icon, requirement, entry cost and effects. Which Agent can it recall and does it automatically give Emperor Influence?', 'Landsraad, 2+ Emperor Influence, 3 Solari. May discard Intrigue to draw Intrigue; recall another Agent and draw card. Not the current Agent. No automatic Emperor Influence.', 'Supplements p2; Main p20','Recall-space requirement versus Faction gain')
add('State Shipping’s access icon, Influence requirement, cost and gains. Does its free-choice Influence have to be with the Guild?', 'Spice Trade, 2+ Guild Influence, 3 spice. Gain 5 Solari and one Influence any one Faction, not necessarily Guild.', 'Supplements p2','Shipping qualifying Faction versus chosen gain')
add('Compare Gather Support and Spice Refinery’s zero-cost and paid options and Combat status.', 'Gather Support Landsraad choose 0/2 Solari, two troops either way, plus one water if paid, not Combat. Refinery City choose 0/1 spice, gain 2/4 Solari respectively, controller 1 Solari either way, Combat.', 'Supplements pp1–2','Optional entry costs and different deployment access')
add('State Heighliner, Desert Tactics and Sardaukar’s entry costs, Influence gains, recruits and other effects; which allow normal deployment?', 'Heighliner 5 spice, Guild Influence +1 and five troops, Combat. Desert Tactics 1 water, Fremen Influence +1 and one troop, optional trash, Combat. Sardaukar 4 spice, Emperor Influence +1 and four troops plus Intrigue, not Combat.', 'Supplements pp1–2','Faction recruit spaces with different Combat flags')
add('What are Assembly Hall, Espionage and Deliver Supplies’s Agent icons, costs and effects, including Assembly Hall’s timing condition?', 'Assembly Hall Landsraad free, Intrigue now, 1 Persuasion at Reveal if own Agent there. Espionage BG 1 spice, 1 BG Influence, card and Spy. Deliver Supplies Guild free, 1 Guild Influence and 1 water. None Combat.', 'Supplements p1','Persistent location conditional and resource/spy spaces')
add('What must False Orders’ affected opponents do, may it be played without an opposing Spy connected to your destination, and when is Litany Against Fear’s red box ignored?', 'Each affected opponent moves Spy to empty observation post not connected to this turn Agent destination. Can play without enemy Spy there. Litany red box ignored during Reveal or with gained Agent icon when played normally as Agent card.', 'FAQ pp2–3 False Orders/Litany Against Fear','Specific movement and card-box exceptions')
add('With Manipulate, may opponents acquire the removed card, may you acquire it by other means with the discount, and when does an unacquired card leave the game?', 'Opponents cannot acquire. You may use other means but 1-Persuasion discount does not apply. If not acquired by end of next Reveal turn, remove from game.', 'FAQ p3 Manipulate','Removed-row card access and expiry')
add('When Combat ends, does Chani treat troops returned to supply as lost, and are multiple sources of retreat or loss combined?', 'Troops returned to supply at Combat resolution count as lost for Chani Leader. Handle each different source of retreating or losing separately.', 'FAQ p1 Chani Leader','Leader loss trigger and source grouping')
# Rival procedures in scope.
add('What components and resource does the standard two-player Rival start with, what happens to the 2P Reshuffle card, and can its 10 VP trigger Endgame and victory?', 'Four cubes at Influence bottoms, three garrison troops rest supply, two Agents supply and third beside board, three Spies and one water supply, score/Combat zero. Retain Reshuffle in Hagal. Scoring Rival can trigger end at 10+ and win.', 'Supplements p3; Main p5','Rival full setup and scoring threat')
add('When does a Rival buy Swordmaster, how does it count and prioritize spending resources, does it keep leftovers, and is its Agent available immediately?', 'As soon as total resources reaches printed value; Solari spice Intrigues water each unit one. Spend only threshold, prioritizing Solari then spice then Intrigue then water; keep leftovers. Third Agent immediately available including current round.', 'Supplements p5; p2 Swordmaster; FAQ p3 Rivals','Automated mixed-resource upgrade timing')
add('After a Rival has Swordmaster, which exact resource sets does it spend for VP, and can it spend a mixed total of seven resources for a VP?', 'Each set 7 Solari, 7 spice, 3 Intrigues or 3 water gives 1 VP whenever available. No mixed seven-resource VP purchase; mixed total only used for Swordmaster.', 'Supplements p5 Buying Victory Points diagram','Rival homogeneous conversion thresholds')
add('When choosing Influence, how does a Rival select the Faction and break ties? Does it get VP at 2 and Alliance VP, or the track bonus at 4? What does a numbered Hagal Influence icon mean?', 'Choose least Influence, ties leftmost priority. Gains/losses of Influence VP and Alliance VP as humans, no 4-track bonus. Number means Faction at that position in printed priority list.', 'Supplements pp4–5; Main p7','Rival priority and track-bonus exception')
add('A Rival reveals a two-destination Hagal card and the condition-selected destination is occupied. Can it use the other destination, and what conditions select these cards?', 'Cannot switch to other; reveal again. Accept Contract/Shipping based on Guild Influence; Deliver Supplies/Heighliner based on Conflict tier I/II/III. Use card printed condition.', 'Supplements p4 Special Instructions; FAQ p3 Rivals','Rival conditional destination cannot fallback')
add('A Rival has no troops newly recruited by a card sending it to Combat. Can it deploy garrison troops? What if a Hagal card recruits at a noncombat space or has a conditional 2-Influence bonus not met?', 'Still deploy up to two available garrison troops at Combat. New troops at noncombat go garrison. Missing 2-Influence bonus does not block placement, just no bonus. Use only Hagal effects, not ordinary board effects.', 'Supplements p4','Rival deployment and conditional bonus failure')
add('How does a Rival choose an unrestricted Spy post, what happens if all Faction posts are occupied, and what occurs on placing its third Spy? Can it Infiltrate or Gather Intelligence?', 'First available Faction post by priority; if all full ignore placement. Third/final supply Spy placed triggers immediately recalling other two and printed Scheme. Never Infiltrate/Gather Intelligence.', 'Supplements pp4–5','Rival automated spy placement and Scheme trigger')
add('If a Rival’s Scheme recruits troops before a Hagal Agent reaches a Combat space on that same turn, what happens to those troops? What if a Place Spy card found no legal post?', 'Deploy Scheme recruits on same-turn Combat placement. Place Spy card still followed by another Hagal reveal whether placement succeeds or not, because no Agent has been sent.', 'Supplements pp4–5','Scheme recruitment timing before placement')
add('At Hagga Basin or Deep Desert, how does a Rival choose worms versus base spice with Hooks, without Hooks, or with a protected Conflict? What happens to accumulated bonus spice?', 'Always take bonus spice. With Hooks and summonable Conflict summons one at Hagga/two Deep instead of base. Without Hooks or if protected, summons none and gains base spice (2/4). At Imperial Basin gains base1. Hagal wall removal requires Hooks.', 'Supplements p5; p4 icons','Rival mandatory worm choice and fallback')
add('When and how is a Rival’s Combat strength bonus determined, what if Reshuffle appears, and can humans respond afterward? Does a unit-free Rival get this bonus?', 'Start Combat in turn order, only with deployed unit: one Hagal card, bottom swords only added. Reshuffle and draw again on Reshuffle. Humans then Combat Intrigue before resolution. No unit no bonus.', 'Supplements p5 Combat','Automated bonus precedes human response')
add('Can a Rival gain control, defensive troops, battle-icon VP and doubled rewards? How does it handle optional Conflict VP payments and contract rewards with CHOAM?', 'Normal control visit bonus and defensive supply troop; win card/match icons; sandworms double. Always buy optional Conflict VP if can pay resources or required Spy recall. Never contracts; each contract reward becomes 2 Solari even with CHOAM.', 'Supplements p5 Combat','Rival reward choices and module exception')
# Freeze v2 with all originals unchanged, using writer definition imported without running v1 writes.
source=(q/'build_bank.py').read_text();namespace={'__file__':str(q/'build_bank.py')};exec(source[:source.index("write('benchmark-v1',rows)")],namespace)
namespace['write']('benchmark-v2',rows)
(q/'bank-rows-v2.json').write_text(json.dumps(rows,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
print(len(rows))
